# Works with the "REST Client" extension in VS Code, Visual Studio 2022 and JetBrains Rider.
# Start the API first:  dotnet run --project src/TenantDesk.Api   (http://localhost:5080)

@host = http://localhost:5080

### Health check (no tenant needed)
GET {{host}}/health

### Acme: create a ticket
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
X-Tenant: acme
X-Api-Key: acme-dev-key
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer on 3rd floor is on fire",
  "description": "Smoke everywhere",
  "priority": "High"
}

### Acme: list tickets
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
X-Tenant: acme
X-Api-Key: acme-dev-key

### Acme: list only open tickets
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?status=Open
X-Tenant: acme
X-Api-Key: acme-dev-key

### Acme: move ticket 1 to InProgress
PATCH {{host}}/api/tickets/1/status
X-Tenant: acme
X-Api-Key: acme-dev-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "InProgress" }

### Globex: its own list - Acme's tickets are NOT visible here
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
X-Tenant: globex
X-Api-Key: globex-dev-key

### Wrong key -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
X-Tenant: acme
X-Api-Key: wrong-key

### No tenant -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
